# Models Folder
# 
# Purpose: Define data structures, database schemas, and data access patterns
# 
# Best Practices:
# - Define TypeScript interfaces/types for your data structures
# - Create database schemas (Mongoose, Prisma, etc.) here
# - One model per database collection/table
# - Include validation rules in model definitions
# - Define relationships between models
# - Export both interfaces/types and model classes
# - Keep models focused on data structure, not business logic
# - Use TypeScript for type safety
# 
# Example structure:
# - poll.model.ts (Poll interface and Mongoose schema)
# - response.model.ts (Response interface and Mongoose schema)
# - user.model.ts (if user authentication is added)

